  "last_message": "I reverted the change \u2014 `docs/features/reminders.md` documents that this was already tried from April\u2013June 2025: 34% of email reminders went unopened, missed pickups rose from 6% to 13%, and volunteers had to throw away uncollected fresh food. SMS was brought back in July 2025 specifically because of that.\n\nBefore touching `reminders.py` again, this would need a real decision to override that documented outcome (e.g., a new ADR or an update to that feature page explaining what's different this time \u2014 cheaper email provider, added SMS fallback only for no-opens, etc.), not just a one-line constant swap. Do you want to:\n\n1. Proceed anyway and switch to email despite the known pickup-rate risk, updating `docs/features/reminders.md` to reflect the new decision and why it's different this time, or\n2. Look for a cheaper way to cut the 40\u20ac/month SMS cost without reverting to email (e.g., renegotiating the provider, reducing reminder volume, SMS only for pickups not yet confirmed)?",
